  "body": "From #109 (commit 08eab1d on issue/109-stale-prior-acquittal, stacked on PR #135).\n\nWhat happens: since #109, every op without a 3+2 frame digests the program ahead of it in its stamp, because its rapid verdict reads that program (the prior acquittal, and the pilot and facing credits). `RegenerateAll::new` stages every Stale op against a frozen world, so a dependent is stamped against its predecessor's OLD cached path. After one click the predecessor reads Ok and the dependent reads Stale. A second click brings it current. This is the M3.1 C two-round convergence Pocket3D already had, but now a plain face-then-contour job hits it too. It is safe: the leftover reads Stale and the post refuses it. It still costs the user a second click.\n\nExpected: one Regenerate All brings the whole job current.\n\nEvidence: `regenerate_all_fixes_the_whole_job_in_one_undo_unit` (crates/app/tests/operations.rs) now asserts two rounds.\n\nDone means: Regenerate All converges in one user action, for example by running rounds until nothing stays Stale, within one undo unit. A test pins that one click leaves Face1 and Contour1 both Ok.\n",
